<title>BULGARIA: BULGARIA INTERNAL CREDIT RISES 2.19 PCT IN WEEK.</title>
<headline>BULGARIA INTERNAL CREDIT RISES 2.19 PCT IN WEEK.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgarian banks' internal credit</p>
<p>rose to 1,267.5 billion levs on November 8 from 1,240.3 billion</p>
<p>levs on November 1, preliminary central bank figures showed.</p>
<p>Credit to government rose by 2.27 percent to 518.7 billion</p>
<p>levs, credit to state firms increased 2.32 percent to 339.9</p>
<p>billion levs and lev-denominated credit to private firms inched</p>
<p>up 0.15 percent to 131.6 billion levs.</p>
<p> PERCENTAGE CHANGE	   NOV8-NOV1  NOV8-OCT25  OCT25-SEPT27</p>
<p> Total internal credit	 +2.19	 +3.38	 +0.50</p>
<p> Credit to govt		  +2.27	 +3.45	 +1.09</p>
<p> Credit to state firms	 +2.32	 +3.69	 +1.05</p>
<p> Lev credit to private firms +0.15	 -0.53	 -1.27</p>
<p> NOMINAL (BILLION LEVS)	 NOV 8	 NOV 1	 OCT 25</p>
<p> Total internal credit	1,267.5     1,240.3	1,226.0</p>
<p> Credit to govt		   518.7	 507.2	  501.4</p>
<p> Credit to state firms	  339.9	 332.2	  327.8</p>
<p> Lev credit to private firms  131.6	 131.4	  132.3</p>
<p> Dlr credit to private firms    1.11	  1.12	   1.11</p>
<p>(USD billion)</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, 359-2-84561</p>
</text>
